      "parameters": {
        "content": "## MCP trigger (added for Phase 11)\n\nThis workflow now exposes TWO MCP tools while keeping the original **Webhook -> Wait for Approval -> Google Docs / Gmail** flow untouched.\n\n**Setup**\n1. Open **MCP Server Trigger**: Authentication = *Bearer Auth*; attach an `httpBearerAuth` credential whose token matches `PULSE_MCP_TOKEN`.\n2. Copy the **Production URL** (`https://<your-n8n>/mcp/weekly-pulse`) into `PULSE_MCP_ENDPOINT` (transport = http).\n3. Credentials on `append_to_note` (Google Docs) and `create_email_draft` (Gmail) are reused from your existing nodes - re-attach them if you import this JSON into a different n8n instance.\n4. **Activate** the workflow, then preflight from the repo root:\n   `python scripts/check_n8n_endpoint.py`\n\n**Do not rename the tool nodes** - the pipeline calls `append_to_note` and `create_email_draft`.\nPublishing is gated by the pipeline approval: Stage G only calls these tools after `--decision approve`.",
